  "summary": "Intel's two-fab leading-edge logic project in New Albany, Licking County, Ohio, announced in January 2022 with an initial investment above $20 billion (later more than $28 billion) and a site that could hold up to eight fabs. Ground was broken in September 2022 and production was first targeted for 2025. In February 2025 Intel slowed construction and moved the first fab (Mod 1) to completion in 2030 with operations in 2030 or 2031, and the second (Mod 2) to 2031 and 2032. In July 2025 it slowed the pace again to match demand. Work continues: in October 2026 Intel reported the first major structural truss set on the first fab.",
